course: dictionary
lesson: 2157
title: Working out a new word from its context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cormorant is a large dark sea bird with a long neck and a hooked beak. When you meet a word you do not know, the words around it can give you clues. «The cormorant dived under the waves and came up with a fish.» Dived and fish tell you that a cormorant hunts under the water.
explain: «The flightless cormorant is the only cormorant that cannot fly; with no land predators and food in the sea, its wings shrank over many generations.» The words that cannot fly tell you that flightless means unable to fly. Check it by swapping in your meaning: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Ask yourself: what kind of thing is this word? Here, cormorant is a noun, a name for a kind of bird. Then ask what the bird does, and the context will tell you more about it.
fact: A cormorant is a noun: a large dark sea bird with a long neck and a hooked beak.
fact: The plural of cormorant is cormorants.
fact: Cormorants dive underwater to catch fish.
fact: Cormorants hold their wings out to dry because their feathers are not fully waterproof.
fact: In China and Japan, people traditionally fished with trained cormorants.
exercise: «The cormorant dived under the waves and came up with a fish.» What does a cormorant do to catch fish? | It sings loudly on the beach | *It dives underwater | It walks on the land | It flies high over the fields
exercise: Why do cormorants hold their wings out after swimming? | *Because their feathers are not fully waterproof, so they dry | To look big to other birds | To wave at the fishermen | To catch the wind and fly away
exercise: «The flightless cormorant is the only cormorant that cannot fly.» What does flightless mean? | Covered in soft feathers | *Unable to fly | Able to fly over the sea | Very fast in the air
test: What is the plural of cormorant? | cormorantses | *cormorants | cormorantes | cormorant-men
test: What is a cormorant? | A small brown land bird that sings in trees | A rock on the beach where birds sit | A kind of fish that swims in rivers | *A large dark sea bird with a long neck and hooked beak
exam: «With no land predators and food in the sea, its wings shrank over many generations.» What does this suggest about the flightless cormorant? | Its wings grew bigger every year to help it fly | The cormorant lost its wings in a storm last week | The cormorant has no wings at all | *Its wings became smaller over time because it did not need to fly
